1
00:00:01,468 --> 00:00:02,302
Ron!

2
00:00:03,803 --> 00:00:05,805
Have you learned your lesson?

3
00:00:07,073 --> 00:00:10,010
You're too old to play mahjong all night.

4
00:00:10,677 --> 00:00:12,245
Don't overdo it.

5
00:00:13,947 --> 00:00:15,715
Where's everyone?

6
00:00:15,782 --> 00:00:16,983
They went home.

7
00:00:18,151 --> 00:00:19,352
No way.

8
00:00:20,587 --> 00:00:22,789
I can't believe this.

9
00:00:23,223 --> 00:00:25,525
I had such a big hand. That's so mean.

10
00:00:25,592 --> 00:00:27,827
You're the one who fell asleep.

11
00:00:27,894 --> 00:00:29,896
You're not young.

12
00:00:29,963 --> 00:00:31,164
Enough.

13
00:00:31,231 --> 00:00:32,132
Yes, sir.

14
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:50,617
Dr. Daimon.
Mr. Yamamoto's exam results are in.

15
00:00:52,018 --> 00:00:52,886
Thanks.

16
00:00:52,952 --> 00:00:54,554
- A CT scan?
- Please.

17
00:00:54,621 --> 00:00:56,556
About Ms. Kimura.

18
00:00:56,623 --> 00:00:58,691
Her surgery will start late.

19
00:00:58,758 --> 00:00:59,893
Alright.

20
00:01:06,499 --> 00:01:07,333
Hey.

21
00:01:08,301 --> 00:01:09,769
Hey, hold on.

22
00:01:10,904 --> 00:01:11,871
Hey!

23
00:01:12,405 --> 00:01:13,239
What?

24
00:01:14,007 --> 00:01:15,275
You dropped it.

25
00:01:15,341 --> 00:01:17,744
You think that girly design is mine?

26
00:01:18,244 --> 00:01:19,913
Excuse me.

27
00:01:21,481 --> 00:01:22,315
You're right.

28
00:01:25,585 --> 00:01:28,822
Dr. Daimon, the patient
has entered the room. Thank you.

29
00:01:28,888 --> 00:01:29,856
Wait.

30
00:01:29,923 --> 00:01:30,990
JUNKO SHIRAKI, HEAD NURSE

31
00:01:31,057 --> 00:01:32,125
Yes?

32
00:01:38,431 --> 00:01:39,265
No way.

33
00:01:47,707 --> 00:01:51,244
This is a story about
a maverick female doctor.

34
00:01:52,278 --> 00:01:53,113
Dr. Fujikawa?

35
00:01:53,179 --> 00:01:54,848
Yes, he just came.

36
00:01:56,883 --> 00:01:58,318
I see.

37
00:01:58,384 --> 00:02:01,855
Transferred Master Yuzuhara here?

38
00:02:01,921 --> 00:02:03,356
I had him come.

39
00:02:03,990 --> 00:02:06,059
I'll cure him

40
00:02:06,392 --> 00:02:09,095
and have him play
in the shogi game championship.

41
00:02:09,162 --> 00:02:10,430
I see.

42
00:02:10,497 --> 00:02:12,732
"The Center's surgical team
revives the master."

43
00:02:12,799 --> 00:02:15,168
That's the scenario.

44
00:02:15,235 --> 00:02:16,369
YOSHIHITO TENDO, PRESIDENT

45
00:02:16,436 --> 00:02:18,104
Scenario?

46
00:02:19,139 --> 00:02:20,540
<i>In 2014,</i>

47
00:02:20,607 --> 00:02:23,743
<i>medical establishments collapsed</i>
<i>and became more corrupt.</i>

48
00:02:23,810 --> 00:02:26,212
<i>Medicine, which handles lives,</i>

49
00:02:26,679 --> 00:02:29,916
<i>had strayed away from what it should be.</i>

50
00:02:30,350 --> 00:02:33,019
I said I'd come at 9AM.

51
00:02:33,086 --> 00:02:36,089
Yes, I did hear that.

52
00:02:36,156 --> 00:02:37,724
It's 9 a.m. now.

53
00:02:38,458 --> 00:02:39,559
It's 9:01.

54
00:02:41,261 --> 00:02:43,796
<i>However, despite these conditions,</i>

55
00:02:44,130 --> 00:02:48,168
<i>Japan announced to export</i>
<i>state of the art medical services</i>

56
00:02:48,234 --> 00:02:50,970
<i>as a growth strategy.</i>

57
00:02:51,037 --> 00:02:52,272
It's quiet.

58
00:02:52,939 --> 00:02:57,377
<i>Healthcare entered an era</i>
<i>of the strong preying on the weak.</i>

59
00:02:58,011 --> 00:02:58,845
Well?

60
00:03:00,880 --> 00:03:01,848
I'll wait.

61
00:03:03,082 --> 00:03:04,083
I'll wait right here.

62
00:03:06,019 --> 00:03:07,253
I can't wait.

63
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:09,155
- Get the purse string suture.
- Yes.

64
00:03:09,222 --> 00:03:13,726
<i>Then came freelance doctors</i>
<i>who don't belong to hospitals.</i>

65
00:03:13,793 --> 00:03:17,497
<i>In other words, maverick doctors.</i>

66
00:03:18,765 --> 00:03:20,900
Hurry with the tissue sealing.

67
00:03:20,967 --> 00:03:21,901
Right away.

68
00:03:21,968 --> 00:03:22,969
Dr. Daimon,

69
00:03:23,036 --> 00:03:25,004
we can't do everything at once.

70
00:03:25,071 --> 00:03:27,273
- Can't you wait?
- I can't.

71
00:03:32,212 --> 00:03:33,279
Dr. Ebina.

72
00:03:33,346 --> 00:03:34,314
Good morning.

73
00:03:34,380 --> 00:03:37,183
Dr. Ebina, why are you here so early?

74
00:03:37,717 --> 00:03:39,552
My article is finished.

75
00:03:39,986 --> 00:03:44,657
"Hybrid NOTES and bevacizumab
for colon cancer."

76
00:03:44,724 --> 00:03:47,794
I'm sorry, I have an appointment.

77
00:03:47,860 --> 00:03:49,495
Let's talk later.

78
00:03:50,563 --> 00:03:51,497
Yes, sir.

79
00:03:52,465 --> 00:03:53,666
Bye.

80
00:03:54,467 --> 00:03:55,301
Bye.

81
00:03:58,137 --> 00:04:00,673
<i>For example, this woman.</i>

82
00:04:01,507 --> 00:04:04,811
<i>She hates groups,</i>
<i>authority, and being controlled.</i>

83
00:04:05,411 --> 00:04:09,749
<i>Her medical license</i>
<i>and experience are her only weapons.</i>

84
00:04:17,590 --> 00:04:19,892
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon, also known as...</i>

85
00:04:20,660 --> 00:04:24,097
<i>Doctor-X.</i>

86
00:04:24,163 --> 00:04:25,231
Could this be...?

87
00:04:37,243 --> 00:04:39,579
The first case is Makoto Yuzuhara,

88
00:04:39,646 --> 00:04:41,180
48 years old, male.

89
00:04:41,714 --> 00:04:44,884
He transferred from Junshinzaka Hospital.

90
00:04:46,152 --> 00:04:49,656
The diagnosis is heart cancer stage III.

91
00:04:50,089 --> 00:04:53,526
A 3cm tumor can be confirmed.

92
00:04:54,193 --> 00:04:56,462
Dr. Fujikawa is the surgeon.

93
00:04:56,529 --> 00:04:59,899
I hear Dr. Ebina's been working all night.

94
00:05:00,700 --> 00:05:04,937
He wants to be recognized
by Mr. Tendo and outdo Dr. Fujikawa.

95
00:05:05,471 --> 00:05:09,375
He's too plain. Fighting too fair.

96
00:05:10,076 --> 00:05:14,280
As you know, Master Yuzuhara is
a star of the shogi game.

97
00:05:14,847 --> 00:05:16,316
With my surgery,

98
00:05:16,382 --> 00:05:19,285
I'll just get rid of the tumor and

99
00:05:19,619 --> 00:05:24,524
have him play in the championship
next month in full health.

100
00:05:25,024 --> 00:05:25,858
Wonderful!

101
00:05:25,925 --> 00:05:27,560
When the master is discharged,

102
00:05:27,627 --> 00:05:29,595
let's call the press.

103
00:05:30,496 --> 00:05:34,233
When it comes to performances,
Fujikawa is better.

104
00:05:34,300 --> 00:05:37,103
People from
western Japan are the pushiest.

105
00:05:37,537 --> 00:05:40,640
I picked this up.

106
00:05:41,474 --> 00:05:43,009
Take it to the office.

107
00:05:43,076 --> 00:05:45,378
Let me operate on this patient.

108
00:05:46,179 --> 00:05:48,715
Another pushy one.

109
00:05:48,781 --> 00:05:50,583
She's here, right?

110
00:05:50,650 --> 00:05:54,320
Judging from the writing,
looks like a grade schooler.

111
00:05:55,254 --> 00:05:58,024
The nurses didn't know her.

112
00:05:58,091 --> 00:06:00,927
- We're in a conference.
- Yes.

113
00:06:00,993 --> 00:06:03,730
She's talking to her mom through writing.

114
00:06:04,364 --> 00:06:05,264
She can't talk.

115
00:06:06,232 --> 00:06:08,067
It says "tube in throat,"

116
00:06:08,134 --> 00:06:09,669
so it's her trachea.

117
00:06:10,103 --> 00:06:11,003
Excuse me.

118
00:06:11,070 --> 00:06:12,238
Look.

119
00:06:14,073 --> 00:06:16,409
It says "whistling noises."

120
00:06:16,476 --> 00:06:18,144
This is stridor.

121
00:06:18,211 --> 00:06:22,682
She has trouble breathing and dizziness.
Last week, she fainted.

122
00:06:22,749 --> 00:06:23,750
Dr. Daimon!

123
00:06:23,816 --> 00:06:27,420
She has pulmonary hypertension.

124
00:06:27,487 --> 00:06:28,454
Correct.

125
00:06:31,224 --> 00:06:35,027
And a rare case.
Pulmonary veno-occlusive disease.

126
00:06:35,628 --> 00:06:37,029
PVOD...

127
00:06:37,764 --> 00:06:38,698
Secretary guy,

128
00:06:38,765 --> 00:06:40,066
show me her charts.

129
00:06:41,934 --> 00:06:45,037
She's a patient of
the guy I filled in for.

130
00:06:45,104 --> 00:06:47,573
Dr. Mango... Tango?

131
00:06:47,640 --> 00:06:51,310
- Dangozaka.
- Yeah, I took her after him,

132
00:06:51,811 --> 00:06:53,212
but I'm having her transfer.

133
00:06:53,279 --> 00:06:54,113
Why?

134
00:06:54,180 --> 00:06:55,381
Why, you ask?

135
00:06:55,748 --> 00:06:57,049
She has a rare disease

136
00:06:57,116 --> 00:07:00,019
with hypoxemia and right heart failure.

137
00:07:02,288 --> 00:07:05,057
There's nothing we can do.

138
00:07:05,124 --> 00:07:05,958
I agree.

139
00:07:06,025 --> 00:07:09,095
It'd be terrible if we let her die.

140
00:07:09,695 --> 00:07:12,298
Yes. So please leave now.

141
00:07:12,365 --> 00:07:13,232
I won't do that.

142
00:07:16,202 --> 00:07:19,038
I'll cut this patient.

143
00:07:19,105 --> 00:07:21,307
You can see her chart later.

144
00:07:22,074 --> 00:07:25,111
Aside from all that, her heart's enlarged.

145
00:07:25,178 --> 00:07:27,713
There's a pulmonary edema risk

146
00:07:27,780 --> 00:07:29,749
with the standard treatment.

147
00:07:30,783 --> 00:07:33,052
A complete cure is impossible.

148
00:07:33,753 --> 00:07:34,687
Not true.

149
00:07:39,292 --> 00:07:40,126
Lung transplant.

150
00:07:41,360 --> 00:07:43,062
Just listen to you.

151
00:07:43,129 --> 00:07:44,697
It'll cure her.

152
00:07:44,764 --> 00:07:46,699
Obviously I know that.

153
00:07:47,166 --> 00:07:49,702
What about the donor?

154
00:07:49,769 --> 00:07:53,439
Will a brain-dead donor
for an 8-year-old pop up?

155
00:07:53,506 --> 00:07:55,541
Living donor lung transplant.

156
00:08:01,614 --> 00:08:05,985
A living donor lung transplant
on an 8-year-old...

157
00:08:06,953 --> 00:08:09,856
- Enough of your jokes.
- Dr. Daimon.

158
00:08:10,223 --> 00:08:13,459
He decided we cannot help her, but...

159
00:08:13,526 --> 00:08:20,399
But I'm trying to cure
this inoperable patient to outdo him?

160
00:08:21,300 --> 00:08:22,969
I have no such intentions.

161
00:08:23,669 --> 00:08:26,005
I just want to help her.

162
00:08:26,539 --> 00:08:32,812
I'm not interested in personal relations
or hierarchies. I'm leaving.

163
00:08:41,621 --> 00:08:45,224
My daughter...
You can really cure Chihiro?

164
00:08:46,425 --> 00:08:47,293
Yes.

165
00:08:51,197 --> 00:08:55,268
Maybe it's fate that I picked this up.

166
00:08:56,235 --> 00:08:59,572
We lost that notebook.

167
00:09:00,506 --> 00:09:03,509
Chihiro, so you did drop it somewhere.

168
00:09:03,576 --> 00:09:05,144
Good thing it's back.

169
00:09:13,719 --> 00:09:14,887
NAME: CHIHIRO

170
00:09:17,590 --> 00:09:18,591
Your dad?

171
00:09:20,092 --> 00:09:24,697
Yes. He died in an accident
right after she was born.

172
00:09:31,737 --> 00:09:34,140
She needs a lung transplant.

173
00:09:34,206 --> 00:09:37,577
Her condition is progressive.

174
00:09:38,010 --> 00:09:39,145
Time's running out.

175
00:09:39,211 --> 00:09:41,280
We can't wait for a brain-dead donor.

176
00:09:42,481 --> 00:09:45,151
Yeah, it could take 6 months.

177
00:09:45,217 --> 00:09:47,353
I can't wait. There's no time.

178
00:09:47,420 --> 00:09:48,921
Here you are, Mai.

179
00:09:48,988 --> 00:09:49,855
HIROMI JONOUCHI, ANESTHETIST

180
00:09:49,922 --> 00:09:53,225
But the girl is 8, so her lung is small.

181
00:09:53,292 --> 00:09:54,760
Cool it down.

182
00:09:54,827 --> 00:09:59,231
An adult donor's lung could be too big.

183
00:09:59,298 --> 00:10:02,335
I'll do a unilateral lung transplant.

184
00:10:02,401 --> 00:10:04,403
Using part of an adult lung...

185
00:10:04,971 --> 00:10:06,172
The mother's?

186
00:10:07,106 --> 00:10:10,476
Her blood type is B, but the girl's is A.

187
00:10:11,277 --> 00:10:13,379
- Father?
- He's dead.

188
00:10:13,980 --> 00:10:14,814
I see.

189
00:10:14,880 --> 00:10:17,216
And they can't ask relatives.

190
00:10:22,455 --> 00:10:27,159
Sometimes, a mother alone
can't do anything no matter what.

191
00:10:30,596 --> 00:10:33,566
Alright. After we eat, I'm going to win!

192
00:10:34,700 --> 00:10:35,534
What?

193
00:10:35,601 --> 00:10:36,769
Mahjong.

194
00:10:38,104 --> 00:10:40,940
It's too ridiculous.

195
00:10:41,340 --> 00:10:45,478
I feel sorry for the girl
who will be the guinea pig

196
00:10:45,544 --> 00:10:46,979
for that surgery addict.

197
00:10:48,047 --> 00:10:49,148
Dr. Fujikawa.

198
00:10:49,215 --> 00:10:50,082
Yes.

199
00:10:50,983 --> 00:10:55,721
I read some of your articles
on regenerative medicine.

200
00:10:55,788 --> 00:10:58,591
They are truly wonderful.

201
00:10:58,658 --> 00:10:59,825
Thank you.

202
00:10:59,892 --> 00:11:00,860
However,

203
00:11:00,926 --> 00:11:04,430
they are still mere scenarios.

204
00:11:06,565 --> 00:11:10,503
The fundamental research
in Japan is at a world-class level.

205
00:11:10,569 --> 00:11:11,570
In other words,

206
00:11:12,138 --> 00:11:14,340
it looks great on paper.

207
00:11:16,275 --> 00:11:21,280
However, there is a dire lack of doctors
who have the skills and courage

208
00:11:21,347 --> 00:11:23,716
to put it into practice.

209
00:11:24,417 --> 00:11:27,620
That is the reality
of healthcare in Japan.

210
00:11:27,687 --> 00:11:28,621
Yeah...

211
00:11:31,590 --> 00:11:32,692
Sir...

212
00:11:33,659 --> 00:11:34,493
So...

213
00:11:35,261 --> 00:11:39,865
if we use a skilled doctor
and build up clinical cases...

214
00:11:39,932 --> 00:11:45,104
Our country can spread the most advanced
healthcare around the world.

215
00:11:46,972 --> 00:11:49,809
That's the story.

216
00:11:57,950 --> 00:12:01,554
What would you like to do? Keep waiting?

217
00:12:04,724 --> 00:12:06,992
I have to make my rounds.

218
00:12:10,796 --> 00:12:14,200
The President hasn't seen Dr. Ebina once.

219
00:12:14,266 --> 00:12:18,204
Oh dear... It mean
she's in favor of Dr. Fujikawa.

220
00:12:19,004 --> 00:12:20,639
I know the type.

221
00:12:20,706 --> 00:12:23,943
They spend their lives waiting
at the back of the line.

222
00:12:27,079 --> 00:12:27,913
KEEP CLOSED

223
00:12:29,348 --> 00:12:30,182
You guys.

224
00:12:33,819 --> 00:12:35,354
- You're here?
- Well,

225
00:12:35,788 --> 00:12:39,058
"Good weather for
a journey will come if you wait."

226
00:12:39,125 --> 00:12:39,959
Journey?

227
00:12:41,093 --> 00:12:43,562
If you be patient and don't fret,

228
00:12:44,396 --> 00:12:48,467
one day, you'll be rewarded with
great weather perfect for a journey.

229
00:12:48,534 --> 00:12:49,602
That's what it means.

230
00:12:50,402 --> 00:12:52,972
Yes, you're exactly right.

231
00:12:53,038 --> 00:12:54,974
Right? In life,

232
00:12:55,040 --> 00:12:57,143
you must believe that and work hard.

233
00:12:57,209 --> 00:12:58,944
You're wrong.

234
00:12:59,445 --> 00:13:00,713
The original saying is

235
00:13:01,147 --> 00:13:04,650
"Sweet nectar will come if you wait."

236
00:13:04,717 --> 00:13:06,152
Nectar?

237
00:13:06,218 --> 00:13:07,953
Sweet nectar like honey.

238
00:13:08,921 --> 00:13:11,357
If you stand in the right spot
with your mouth open,

239
00:13:11,423 --> 00:13:14,927
nectar will come falling down.

240
00:13:15,494 --> 00:13:17,163
A journey?

241
00:13:17,229 --> 00:13:20,733
You don't have to
go through all that trouble.

242
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:22,902
I see.

243
00:13:22,968 --> 00:13:24,770
It's about where you stand.

244
00:13:40,219 --> 00:13:43,088
Mr. Tendo's here, right?

245
00:13:43,756 --> 00:13:45,224
He went out.

246
00:13:46,525 --> 00:13:47,726
Good day.

247
00:13:52,431 --> 00:13:55,267
But I'm trying to cure

248
00:13:55,334 --> 00:13:59,271
this inoperable patient to outdo him?

249
00:14:03,609 --> 00:14:06,879
A relative who could
be a donor for Chihiro?

250
00:14:06,946 --> 00:14:07,780
Anyone?

251
00:14:09,348 --> 00:14:11,617
I overheard before...

252
00:14:12,685 --> 00:14:15,454
They fought with
their relatives over money.

253
00:14:16,121 --> 00:14:20,726
So they haven't been
keeping in touch with them.

254
00:14:20,793 --> 00:14:21,994
A debt?

255
00:14:22,361 --> 00:14:23,896
I saw that before,

256
00:14:24,496 --> 00:14:25,531
at the public phone.

257
00:14:25,598 --> 00:14:27,433
So did I.

258
00:14:27,499 --> 00:14:29,101
<i>She was apologizing about money.</i>

259
00:14:29,168 --> 00:14:31,103
<i>She kept saying sorry.</i>

260
00:14:31,170 --> 00:14:32,771
I'm so sorry.

261
00:14:35,808 --> 00:14:36,642
I see.

262
00:14:37,543 --> 00:14:42,047
Do not give the patients false hope.
I told you.

263
00:14:42,114 --> 00:14:44,583
A super doctor like you is the worst.

264
00:14:44,650 --> 00:14:46,218
She never listens.

265
00:14:46,285 --> 00:14:48,420
Yeah, she's hopeless.

266
00:14:48,487 --> 00:14:50,656
PEDIATRICS

267
00:14:50,723 --> 00:14:52,024
See you tomorrow.

268
00:15:02,134 --> 00:15:04,336
If only we could find a donor.

269
00:15:04,770 --> 00:15:07,907
I'm sorry.
I'm not keeping in touch with relatives.

270
00:15:09,441 --> 00:15:11,377
- Anyone you can ask?
- No.

271
00:15:14,313 --> 00:15:15,314
Please.

272
00:15:16,482 --> 00:15:21,086
Could you find someone?

273
00:15:21,153 --> 00:15:24,590
There are plenty of people
whose blood type is A.

274
00:15:26,392 --> 00:15:29,428
Won't someone give my daughter a lung?

275
00:15:30,195 --> 00:15:34,233
A living donor has to be
a relative to be compatible.

276
00:15:54,787 --> 00:15:55,788
Anyways,

277
00:15:56,622 --> 00:15:59,491
I'm sure that even if I tell you this,

278
00:15:59,892 --> 00:16:03,228
you'll just say,
"Don't care. Not interested."

279
00:16:07,566 --> 00:16:12,471
Don't be like this. The patient might not
be able to pay the medical bills.

280
00:16:13,439 --> 00:16:16,108
If they can't...

281
00:16:16,842 --> 00:16:22,081
Will you take responsibility, Dr. Daimon?

282
00:16:24,016 --> 00:16:25,117
I won't do that.

283
00:16:51,477 --> 00:16:52,644
What's going on?

284
00:16:54,046 --> 00:16:56,382
I found this in the hall before.

285
00:16:59,618 --> 00:17:01,220
You didn't drop it,

286
00:17:02,588 --> 00:17:04,323
but you threw it away on purpose?

287
00:17:18,037 --> 00:17:20,606
PLEASE THROW THIS AWAY

288
00:17:20,672 --> 00:17:23,575
Why? You need this
to talk with your mom...

289
00:17:29,982 --> 00:17:32,418
I don't get it. Sorry.

290
00:17:32,484 --> 00:17:36,288
She's not fighting
with her mom in writing.

291
00:17:36,355 --> 00:17:37,189
Right?

292
00:17:39,892 --> 00:17:42,861
Who could it be at this hour?

293
00:17:50,035 --> 00:17:51,036
A melon?

294
00:17:51,103 --> 00:17:51,970
No.

295
00:17:53,205 --> 00:17:54,907
MANGO

296
00:17:55,307 --> 00:17:56,842
- Mango.
- Mango?

297
00:17:57,743 --> 00:17:58,610
What do you want?

298
00:18:06,952 --> 00:18:11,457
We might as well call Hiromi
and play a game.

299
00:18:11,523 --> 00:18:12,624
Let's do it.

300
00:18:12,991 --> 00:18:16,662
No, I've never played mahjong before.

301
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:22,835
So...

302
00:18:24,236 --> 00:18:27,106
Have you found someone
for the living donor lung transplant?

303
00:18:27,172 --> 00:18:28,340
Not yet.

304
00:18:29,875 --> 00:18:31,376
Is your blood type A?

305
00:18:32,377 --> 00:18:33,712
Are you a relative?

306
00:18:34,413 --> 00:18:37,015
You don't smoke.

307
00:18:37,449 --> 00:18:39,017
No, that's not it.

308
00:18:39,084 --> 00:18:40,419
Then what?

309
00:18:42,521 --> 00:18:43,355
Well...

310
00:18:45,190 --> 00:18:48,794
If you find a donor
and she's going to get surgery...

311
00:18:50,529 --> 00:18:52,831
I can do it for you.

312
00:18:54,566 --> 00:18:56,702
It's not my specialty, but I can do it.

313
00:18:57,436 --> 00:18:59,104
Daimon.

314
00:19:00,539 --> 00:19:04,309
- I'd let you be my assistant.
- What are you talking about?

315
00:19:05,711 --> 00:19:07,713
Well I came to talk to you...

316
00:19:07,779 --> 00:19:12,050
Or propose that idea to you.

317
00:19:12,117 --> 00:19:13,085
So I came.

318
00:19:13,152 --> 00:19:14,419
I won't do that.

319
00:19:16,321 --> 00:19:19,858
You want to outdo Fujikawa, who you hate.

320
00:19:20,726 --> 00:19:21,627
That's not it...

321
00:19:21,693 --> 00:19:24,496
I won't assist in power struggles.

322
00:19:24,563 --> 00:19:25,998
I said that's not it.

323
00:19:27,366 --> 00:19:28,200
Well...

324
00:19:33,105 --> 00:19:33,972
You're right.

325
00:19:35,974 --> 00:19:36,808
You're right.

326
00:19:38,277 --> 00:19:39,311
You got a problem?

327
00:19:41,413 --> 00:19:46,351
With Dangozaka gone
and the surgery department unified,

328
00:19:49,288 --> 00:19:51,456
I thought my time to rule had come.

329
00:19:52,925 --> 00:19:53,926
But then came Fujikawa.

330
00:19:55,661 --> 00:19:56,562
It's a joke.

331
00:19:59,498 --> 00:20:00,666
Don't you think so?

332
00:20:00,732 --> 00:20:01,667
I don't.

333
00:20:03,168 --> 00:20:04,570
You're just a part-timer.

334
00:20:04,636 --> 00:20:05,938
Freelancer.

335
00:20:08,273 --> 00:20:09,942
Dr. Ebina.

336
00:20:12,177 --> 00:20:14,479
- Yes.
- Let's go out.

337
00:20:17,049 --> 00:20:18,116
What?

338
00:20:34,499 --> 00:20:36,268
I used to come to these a lot.

339
00:20:38,036 --> 00:20:39,571
Public baths never change.

340
00:20:40,672 --> 00:20:42,574
The new spas they have lately,

341
00:20:42,941 --> 00:20:44,776
they lack atmosphere.

342
00:20:47,379 --> 00:20:48,413
Dr. Ebina.

343
00:20:50,048 --> 00:20:50,916
Yes?

344
00:20:51,917 --> 00:20:56,255
Why do you think Michiko
always says reckless things?

345
00:20:58,624 --> 00:21:00,993
"I don't fail."

346
00:21:05,831 --> 00:21:07,132
It's determination.

347
00:21:09,201 --> 00:21:14,306
For the patient,
one failure and it's over.

348
00:21:16,475 --> 00:21:20,379
But doctors just think that
they'll try to not fail the next time.

349
00:21:20,979 --> 00:21:23,915
- That's what she thinks.
- Any doctor would...

350
00:21:23,982 --> 00:21:28,587
Listen.
Michiko isn't some ordinary doctor.

351
00:21:30,989 --> 00:21:35,427
And you're telling Michiko
that you'll do it?

352
00:21:36,228 --> 00:21:37,629
You'll make her an assistant?

353
00:21:39,131 --> 00:21:40,766
How dare you.

354
00:21:46,038 --> 00:21:49,875
I can't say this when Michiko is around.

355
00:21:52,944 --> 00:21:58,550
Public baths sure are great.

356
00:22:13,365 --> 00:22:15,934
PLEASE THROW THIS AWAY

357
00:22:17,302 --> 00:22:18,970
I don't get it.

358
00:23:00,679 --> 00:23:02,180
Unbelievable.

359
00:23:05,917 --> 00:23:07,052
Really?

360
00:23:08,353 --> 00:23:09,187
Yes.

361
00:23:10,455 --> 00:23:12,958
I'm Chihiro's father.

362
00:23:14,526 --> 00:23:15,460
But why?

363
00:23:17,662 --> 00:23:20,465
I started gambling and made a huge debt.

364
00:23:22,768 --> 00:23:26,037
I left Kazumi and my newly born Chihiro...

365
00:23:27,873 --> 00:23:28,707
And ran away.

366
00:23:30,542 --> 00:23:34,980
For 7 years after that,
I barely made a living.

367
00:23:36,047 --> 00:23:37,115
But around last year,

368
00:23:37,682 --> 00:23:39,317
I became a cab driver

369
00:23:39,785 --> 00:23:41,520
and was able to live properly.

370
00:23:42,454 --> 00:23:46,091
I went and asked a relative about

371
00:23:46,158 --> 00:23:48,994
how Kazumi and Chihiro were doing.

372
00:23:49,461 --> 00:23:53,398
Then I heard that Chihiro was very ill.

373
00:23:54,299 --> 00:23:57,769
I found out where she was
and went when Kazumi wasn't there.

374
00:24:03,041 --> 00:24:05,777
Sorry I scared you.

375
00:24:08,847 --> 00:24:12,184
You probably don't know who I am.

376
00:24:23,695 --> 00:24:25,964
DAD

377
00:24:37,242 --> 00:24:39,277
NAME: CHIHIRO

378
00:24:55,327 --> 00:24:56,194
DAD: WHY?

379
00:24:56,261 --> 00:24:59,064
My wife told Chihiro that

380
00:24:59,130 --> 00:25:04,135
her father died in
an accident after she was born.

381
00:25:05,437 --> 00:25:06,905
Of course.

382
00:25:07,506 --> 00:25:09,574
Having a useless father like me

383
00:25:10,375 --> 00:25:12,043
would be too terrible for her.

384
00:25:12,811 --> 00:25:15,981
After that, I'd secretly go see her

385
00:25:16,047 --> 00:25:17,983
when Kazumi wasn't around.

386
00:25:18,049 --> 00:25:18,917
Excuse me,

387
00:25:19,284 --> 00:25:21,086
- another cafe latte.
- Yes.

388
00:25:21,720 --> 00:25:25,257
<i>I told her she could call any time.</i>
<i>I gave her my number.</i>

389
00:25:31,429 --> 00:25:33,798
She was trying to throw this away?

390
00:25:33,865 --> 00:25:34,866
Excuse me.

391
00:25:34,933 --> 00:25:36,601
Hurry up with my latte.

392
00:25:36,668 --> 00:25:37,502
Yes.

393
00:25:38,236 --> 00:25:42,974
She didn't want her mother
to find out I was seeing her.

394
00:25:43,775 --> 00:25:46,311
Yours might be too big.

395
00:25:46,912 --> 00:25:47,746
What?

396
00:25:48,547 --> 00:25:49,648
Let's just go.

397
00:25:50,348 --> 00:25:52,317
I can't wait.

398
00:25:52,384 --> 00:25:54,119
Cancel the latte.

399
00:25:57,622 --> 00:26:00,859
What do you want to hear about Dad today?

400
00:26:02,627 --> 00:26:04,996
Where's the notebook?

401
00:26:08,600 --> 00:26:09,634
What happened?

402
00:26:10,268 --> 00:26:11,770
It's hard without that.

403
00:26:12,203 --> 00:26:13,772
I'll go buy a new one.

404
00:26:17,909 --> 00:26:18,944
Chihiro?

405
00:26:19,678 --> 00:26:20,912
Are you okay?

406
00:26:21,947 --> 00:26:22,814
Chihiro.

407
00:26:25,250 --> 00:26:26,952
Dr. Daimon. It's Chihiro.

408
00:26:29,654 --> 00:26:30,555
Yes?

409
00:26:30,622 --> 00:26:32,557
Epoprostenol and bozentan.

410
00:26:32,624 --> 00:26:34,159
Get the PCPS too.

411
00:26:37,629 --> 00:26:39,764
Her heart failure is advanced.

412
00:26:39,831 --> 00:26:42,133
Her heart could stop.

413
00:26:44,469 --> 00:26:45,837
We can't wait.

414
00:26:45,904 --> 00:26:47,739
We need a lung transplant.

415
00:26:49,741 --> 00:26:50,575
But...

416
00:26:51,009 --> 00:26:52,811
I found a donor.

417
00:26:55,714 --> 00:26:56,815
Really?

418
00:27:01,186 --> 00:27:02,621
Who is it?

419
00:27:02,687 --> 00:27:04,189
They wish to be anonymous.

420
00:27:08,893 --> 00:27:10,929
Unilateral lung transplant.

421
00:27:10,996 --> 00:27:14,299
The donor's right lower lobe
will be her right lung.

422
00:27:14,699 --> 00:27:17,168
We can leave her left lung.

423
00:27:17,235 --> 00:27:19,037
Doctor!

424
00:27:19,104 --> 00:27:22,507
Isn't the donor's body way too big?

425
00:27:23,041 --> 00:27:23,975
Yes.

426
00:27:24,676 --> 00:27:29,347
Even if it's just his right lower lobe,
isn't it too big?

427
00:27:29,414 --> 00:27:33,818
Her thorax is even smaller
from the enlarged heart.

428
00:27:33,885 --> 00:27:35,520
It won't fit.

429
00:27:36,021 --> 00:27:39,457
I'll have 2 assistants.
Who's the 1st assistant?

430
00:27:42,360 --> 00:27:44,129
I'll do it.

431
00:27:44,729 --> 00:27:46,898
Dr. Hara, please be the 2nd.

432
00:27:47,666 --> 00:27:49,534
You'll extract the donor's graft.

433
00:27:50,168 --> 00:27:51,703
Demon, no.

434
00:27:51,770 --> 00:27:53,038
Don't get me involved.

435
00:27:53,104 --> 00:27:57,475
Start once the patient
has been safely anesthetized.

436
00:27:57,542 --> 00:27:58,743
Thank you.

437
00:27:58,810 --> 00:27:59,811
Yes.

438
00:28:01,312 --> 00:28:03,515
Dr. Ebina.

439
00:28:03,581 --> 00:28:05,817
I'm busy. Make it later.

440
00:28:05,884 --> 00:28:06,885
It's Mr. Tendo.

441
00:28:07,452 --> 00:28:08,453
Mr. Tendo?

442
00:28:08,520 --> 00:28:12,290
He wanted you to call,
but if you're busy...

443
00:28:13,358 --> 00:28:15,260
Wait. Hold on.

444
00:28:15,326 --> 00:28:18,129
Yes, the report...wait...

445
00:28:18,196 --> 00:28:20,899
I'll have time at 6 today.

446
00:28:21,499 --> 00:28:22,333
What do you think?

447
00:28:22,667 --> 00:28:26,037
How about we have dinner
and I'll see what you wrote?

448
00:28:27,005 --> 00:28:28,006
Yes, sir.

449
00:28:28,073 --> 00:28:29,240
6 o'clock?

450
00:28:29,307 --> 00:28:31,976
I'll be done with the surgery by then.

451
00:28:32,544 --> 00:28:34,746
Where shall we go?

452
00:28:34,813 --> 00:28:37,649
Any good places you know?

453
00:28:37,716 --> 00:28:40,418
How's Omiya in Sukiyabashi?

454
00:28:41,386 --> 00:28:44,289
I know that place.
So you're a regular there?

455
00:28:44,355 --> 00:28:45,824
Yes.

456
00:28:45,890 --> 00:28:48,059
Please hold.

457
00:28:48,426 --> 00:28:49,627
Sekigahara!

458
00:28:49,694 --> 00:28:52,464
Six o'clock at Omiya.
Make a reservation for two.

459
00:28:52,530 --> 00:28:53,465
The main branch.

460
00:28:54,032 --> 00:28:59,137
Hello? I will be there 10 minutes early.

461
00:29:05,610 --> 00:29:08,446
Don't worry. Everything will be fine.

462
00:29:11,783 --> 00:29:13,451
This is Chihiro Hatta.

463
00:29:13,518 --> 00:29:14,786
Sorry for the trouble.

464
00:29:14,853 --> 00:29:17,722
Excuse me. Let's get prepared.

465
00:29:18,456 --> 00:29:19,324
Yes.

466
00:29:22,360 --> 00:29:24,496
Let's get this over with quickly.

467
00:29:24,562 --> 00:29:26,064
You're always quick.

468
00:29:26,831 --> 00:29:28,366
You're in a good mood.

469
00:29:28,433 --> 00:29:30,568
I'm normal.

470
00:29:43,615 --> 00:29:46,151
Anesthetics administered. No problems.

471
00:29:46,818 --> 00:29:47,986
Vitals stable.

472
00:29:48,052 --> 00:29:49,687
- Call them.
- Yes.

473
00:29:49,754 --> 00:29:51,623
Contacting surgery room B.

474
00:29:52,524 --> 00:29:54,592
- Hurry.
- Yes.

475
00:29:56,327 --> 00:29:58,963
This is surgery room A. We will begin.

476
00:30:00,765 --> 00:30:03,735
Right segmental lung transplant.

477
00:30:03,802 --> 00:30:05,170
First, extract the right lung.

478
00:30:05,236 --> 00:30:06,171
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

479
00:30:09,240 --> 00:30:12,210
OPERATION ROOM

480
00:30:20,718 --> 00:30:22,320
Room A has started.

481
00:30:22,387 --> 00:30:24,956
I will extract the lung's graft.

482
00:30:25,423 --> 00:30:28,226
Intercostal space 5
posterolateral thoracotomy.

483
00:30:28,993 --> 00:30:30,595
- Let's begin.
- Please.

484
00:30:30,662 --> 00:30:31,663
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

485
00:30:35,533 --> 00:30:37,769
Here are the exam results.

486
00:30:38,336 --> 00:30:40,071
The ACT is over 400.

487
00:30:40,138 --> 00:30:41,573
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

488
00:30:54,185 --> 00:30:56,221
- Cardiopulmonary bypass.
- Yes.

489
00:31:01,226 --> 00:31:02,560
Stopping ventilation.

490
00:31:05,196 --> 00:31:07,131
I'll cut the pulmonary vein and artery.

491
00:31:07,198 --> 00:31:08,399
- Satinsky.
- Yes.

492
00:31:13,771 --> 00:31:14,939
- Metzenbaum.
- Yes.

493
00:31:18,743 --> 00:31:20,278
What was he thinking?

494
00:31:20,345 --> 00:31:22,180
Fujikawa could at least come and watch.

495
00:31:23,248 --> 00:31:24,515
That's so funny.

496
00:31:25,550 --> 00:31:26,918
That's hilarious!

497
00:31:27,352 --> 00:31:30,021
They're not funny at all.

498
00:31:30,722 --> 00:31:32,223
How stupid.

499
00:31:33,024 --> 00:31:35,159
Eastern Japan's comedy is terrible.

500
00:31:49,240 --> 00:31:50,642
Lung extracted.

501
00:31:50,708 --> 00:31:52,176
You sure are fast.

502
00:31:52,710 --> 00:31:54,512
You're excessively happy.

503
00:31:54,579 --> 00:31:56,347
Excessively?

504
00:31:56,748 --> 00:31:57,982
Where's the graft?

505
00:31:58,049 --> 00:31:58,950
I can't wait.

506
00:31:59,017 --> 00:32:01,419
You should learn how to wait.

507
00:32:01,486 --> 00:32:03,254
- I can't.
- Just wait.

508
00:32:07,692 --> 00:32:08,893
The graft is coming.

509
00:32:19,170 --> 00:32:20,638
This is...

510
00:32:20,705 --> 00:32:22,573
It's bigger than I thought.

511
00:32:25,243 --> 00:32:27,345
Will it fit in her right chest?

512
00:32:29,514 --> 00:32:32,150
I'll join the bronchial tubes.
4-0 sutures.

513
00:32:35,520 --> 00:32:36,621
- Metzenbaum.
- Yes.

514
00:32:37,922 --> 00:32:40,425
Next is the pulmonary vein.

515
00:32:40,825 --> 00:32:41,993
- 7-0 nylon.
- Yes.

516
00:32:51,002 --> 00:32:51,936
That's fast.

517
00:32:53,805 --> 00:32:55,406
We'll be done by 5.

518
00:32:58,810 --> 00:33:02,046
Lung artery declamped. Restart blood flow.

519
00:33:02,113 --> 00:33:03,047
Yes.

520
00:33:04,916 --> 00:33:06,184
Reventilating.

521
00:33:13,992 --> 00:33:15,593
Good.

522
00:33:15,660 --> 00:33:17,562
Air is being sent to the new lung.

523
00:33:17,628 --> 00:33:19,030
It's regaining color.

524
00:33:23,434 --> 00:33:24,635
This is bad.

525
00:33:26,104 --> 00:33:28,139
The graft is swelling.

526
00:33:29,374 --> 00:33:30,274
Really?

527
00:33:35,179 --> 00:33:37,582
- Hey!
- It's sticking out of her chest.

528
00:33:37,949 --> 00:33:40,184
The graft is too big.

529
00:33:40,251 --> 00:33:42,820
There's no way it'll fit.

530
00:33:42,887 --> 00:33:44,889
We can't even close her up.

531
00:33:44,956 --> 00:33:46,891
- Check the blood gas.
- Yes.

532
00:33:55,833 --> 00:33:56,968
The results are here.

533
00:33:58,870 --> 00:34:01,739
CO2 42 and O2 170.

534
00:34:04,108 --> 00:34:06,210
Her heart is pushing the lung.

535
00:34:07,478 --> 00:34:08,513
What now?

536
00:34:12,083 --> 00:34:13,251
What are you going to do?

537
00:34:14,919 --> 00:34:16,187
Daimon, what can we do?

538
00:34:30,535 --> 00:34:32,470
- We'll wait.
- Wait?

539
00:34:34,839 --> 00:34:37,408
What?

540
00:34:38,810 --> 00:34:39,710
Hold on.

541
00:34:41,079 --> 00:34:42,180
Daimon!

542
00:34:53,758 --> 00:34:54,592
Daimon.

543
00:34:56,694 --> 00:34:59,063
Wait?

544
00:35:00,965 --> 00:35:02,333
What are we going to wait for?

545
00:35:03,367 --> 00:35:04,202
I don't know.

546
00:35:04,268 --> 00:35:05,870
You don't know?

547
00:35:06,604 --> 00:35:07,438
Listen...

548
00:35:11,142 --> 00:35:12,710
I'll have time at 6 today.

549
00:35:12,777 --> 00:35:15,046
I'll see what you wrote.

550
00:35:20,551 --> 00:35:22,620
It's fine. I still have over an hour.

551
00:35:29,427 --> 00:35:31,963
30 MINUTES LATER

552
00:35:35,700 --> 00:35:36,801
Please.

553
00:35:37,502 --> 00:35:39,871
Same. Blood gas?

554
00:35:39,937 --> 00:35:42,173
CO2 40, O2 178.

555
00:35:42,640 --> 00:35:46,410
If you extract the left lung,
the graft will fit.

556
00:35:47,044 --> 00:35:49,347
- The left lung stays.
- Why?

557
00:35:49,413 --> 00:35:51,382
It's functioning.

558
00:35:51,449 --> 00:35:53,417
I won't remove a healthy organ.

559
00:35:59,190 --> 00:36:00,691
Just close her skin.

560
00:36:00,758 --> 00:36:03,027
What will that do?

561
00:36:03,628 --> 00:36:04,962
X-ray in 30 minutes.

562
00:36:05,029 --> 00:36:05,997
30 minutes?

563
00:36:06,063 --> 00:36:07,198
Wait until then.

564
00:36:07,265 --> 00:36:08,599
Hey!

565
00:36:08,666 --> 00:36:09,834
Just sit around?

566
00:36:09,901 --> 00:36:11,068
For what?

567
00:36:11,435 --> 00:36:13,905
That's the opposite of what you always do.

568
00:36:32,790 --> 00:36:33,691
It's over.

569
00:37:05,356 --> 00:37:06,290
Hey.

570
00:37:08,759 --> 00:37:10,094
It's determination.

571
00:37:10,161 --> 00:37:15,666
For the patient,
one failure and it's over.

572
00:37:29,013 --> 00:37:30,147
Please come.

573
00:37:39,457 --> 00:37:41,892
- Look.
- Her heart shrunk.

574
00:37:42,260 --> 00:37:44,528
- No way.
- The graft is functioning.

575
00:37:47,365 --> 00:37:48,599
It'll fit now.

576
00:37:48,666 --> 00:37:51,335
Her heart and lung are smaller.

577
00:37:51,402 --> 00:37:53,104
Remove the temporary sutures.

578
00:37:58,309 --> 00:37:59,176
Wow...

579
00:37:59,610 --> 00:38:01,445
The graft is fitting in the thorax.

580
00:38:01,512 --> 00:38:03,347
I can close her breastbone too.

581
00:38:04,148 --> 00:38:05,883
- I'll close it now.
- Yes.

582
00:38:42,687 --> 00:38:43,788
Done.

583
00:38:56,834 --> 00:38:57,702
Thanks.

584
00:38:58,769 --> 00:39:00,237
Thank you.

585
00:39:04,475 --> 00:39:05,643
It's 6:30.

586
00:39:07,078 --> 00:39:08,412
5 hours total.

587
00:39:09,347 --> 00:39:11,482
Was that fast or not?

588
00:39:13,384 --> 00:39:14,518
It's probably fast.

589
00:39:22,626 --> 00:39:24,495
I see.

590
00:39:27,631 --> 00:39:28,499
Thank you.

591
00:39:37,208 --> 00:39:39,043
It's not over yet?

592
00:39:39,110 --> 00:39:42,380
The transplant
that Dr. Ebina is assisting.

593
00:39:42,780 --> 00:39:44,882
They just finished.

594
00:39:46,317 --> 00:39:49,120
The graft was said to be too big,

595
00:39:49,186 --> 00:39:53,023
but after just an hour,
her enlarged heart got better.

596
00:39:53,657 --> 00:39:56,994
It all fit in her thorax.

597
00:39:57,061 --> 00:40:00,331
By waiting?

598
00:40:00,398 --> 00:40:01,832
Now...

599
00:40:02,666 --> 00:40:05,569
we have another clinical example.

600
00:40:07,505 --> 00:40:10,541
I understand very well now...

601
00:40:11,742 --> 00:40:13,611
How to use that woman.

602
00:40:16,781 --> 00:40:18,549
I don't know where she learned,

603
00:40:19,550 --> 00:40:20,684
but Michiko Daimon...

604
00:40:21,719 --> 00:40:23,387
is very skilled.

605
00:40:24,622 --> 00:40:26,490
You're very right.

606
00:40:30,861 --> 00:40:35,833
She did save a patient you abandoned.

607
00:41:17,608 --> 00:41:18,476
Sorry,

608
00:41:19,610 --> 00:41:21,912
I wasn't going to come forward.

609
00:41:25,216 --> 00:41:26,050
But Kazumi...

610
00:41:30,354 --> 00:41:31,422
I wanted to see you.

611
00:41:34,859 --> 00:41:35,893
Can you even imagine

612
00:41:38,028 --> 00:41:42,933
how hard these past 7 years were?

613
00:41:46,704 --> 00:41:48,672
Just because you saved Chihiro...

614
00:41:50,875 --> 00:41:52,676
It doesn't make everything right.

615
00:41:58,883 --> 00:41:59,717
Of course...

616
00:42:02,019 --> 00:42:04,655
Of course you're going to save her.

617
00:42:08,325 --> 00:42:09,460
You're...

618
00:42:12,596 --> 00:42:14,064
Her father.

619
00:42:19,970 --> 00:42:20,938
Kazumi.

620
00:42:25,910 --> 00:42:27,511
Thank you, honey.

621
00:42:29,446 --> 00:42:33,417
I've been waiting for so long.

622
00:42:33,851 --> 00:42:34,919
Kazumi.

623
00:42:39,189 --> 00:42:40,324
Honey.

624
00:42:58,709 --> 00:43:00,277
A CASE REPORT OF PULMONARY
VENO-OCCLUSIVE DISEASE

625
00:43:01,912 --> 00:43:05,249
I will write an article
based on the transplant.

626
00:43:05,983 --> 00:43:07,918
Get an appointment with Mr. Tendo.

627
00:43:07,985 --> 00:43:09,186
Yes.

628
00:43:10,054 --> 00:43:12,590
But it seems the President is very busy.

629
00:43:14,592 --> 00:43:16,961
It can be any time. I'll wait.

630
00:43:18,829 --> 00:43:20,497
Good weather comes if you wait.

631
00:43:21,899 --> 00:43:24,234
I won't just stand there
with my mouth open.

632
00:43:26,470 --> 00:43:27,771
This is a bill.

633
00:43:29,039 --> 00:43:30,007
This is a melon.

634
00:43:33,711 --> 00:43:34,645
Mr. Kanbara.

635
00:43:35,012 --> 00:43:35,879
Yes.

636
00:43:36,647 --> 00:43:42,286
I think there's a need
to reconsider this price.

637
00:43:43,287 --> 00:43:47,558
It's true that we accepted on our own,
surgery for a patient

638
00:43:47,925 --> 00:43:50,094
with financial problems.

639
00:43:50,527 --> 00:43:51,395
However...

640
00:43:51,462 --> 00:43:52,630
Excuse me.

641
00:43:53,664 --> 00:43:54,598
Michiko?

642
00:43:54,999 --> 00:43:57,568
I called her here.

643
00:43:59,069 --> 00:44:03,073
I'd like to talk about
the current contract.

644
00:44:03,140 --> 00:44:04,608
At this point in time?

645
00:44:04,675 --> 00:44:05,676
Ms. Daimon.

646
00:44:06,577 --> 00:44:09,079
Another great surgery.

647
00:44:09,947 --> 00:44:10,781
Thanks.

648
00:44:10,848 --> 00:44:12,750
You are extremely skilled.

649
00:44:13,484 --> 00:44:16,720
You will surely create
more clinical examples

650
00:44:16,787 --> 00:44:20,991
to contribute to
the future of Japan's healthcare.

651
00:44:22,960 --> 00:44:23,994
From now on,

652
00:44:24,728 --> 00:44:27,698
we will double your contract money.

653
00:44:28,532 --> 00:44:29,533
What?

654
00:44:29,600 --> 00:44:35,205
No matter how much the fee is,
you were worth installing.

655
00:44:35,839 --> 00:44:37,007
Install?

656
00:44:37,608 --> 00:44:42,579
You are an excellent... Surgery machine.

657
00:44:43,247 --> 00:44:44,281
Machine?

658
00:44:44,348 --> 00:44:49,053
Currently, you are
a machine of the latest model.

659
00:44:50,621 --> 00:44:51,555
Excuse me...

660
00:44:51,622 --> 00:44:54,625
I will follow the instructions carefully

661
00:44:55,125 --> 00:45:00,097
and handle you properly.

662
00:45:00,164 --> 00:45:01,832
Therefore, I ask the owner...

663
00:45:01,899 --> 00:45:05,269
- Owner?
- to carry out proper maintenance.

664
00:45:07,337 --> 00:45:08,439
That is all.

665
00:45:28,058 --> 00:45:31,829
<i>She hates groups,</i>
<i>authority, and being controlled.</i>

666
00:45:32,996 --> 00:45:33,931
Michiko.

667
00:45:36,166 --> 00:45:40,537
<i>Her medical license</i>
<i>and experience are her only weapons.</i>

668
00:45:43,540 --> 00:45:45,309
How could he put it like that?

669
00:45:46,343 --> 00:45:48,112
Talking like you're disposable.

670
00:45:51,982 --> 00:45:53,016
Akira.

671
00:45:58,088 --> 00:45:59,990
Take me to maintenance.

672
00:46:00,057 --> 00:46:01,024
What?

673
00:46:01,091 --> 00:46:03,660
I need oil. Beef!

674
00:46:04,061 --> 00:46:07,865
Fatty beef.

675
00:46:07,931 --> 00:46:10,100
Let's go.

676
00:46:10,167 --> 00:46:13,437
That's all you talk about.

677
00:46:24,248 --> 00:46:27,151
Skirt steak. Ribs. Hurry!

678
00:46:27,217 --> 00:46:30,521
- Michiko, wait.
- I can't wait.

679
00:46:30,587 --> 00:46:34,525
You're so obnoxious. Why can't you wait?

680
00:46:34,591 --> 00:46:38,462
I can't wait. Hurry up.

681
00:46:38,529 --> 00:46:40,497
They're cutting the meat.

682
00:46:40,931 --> 00:46:41,765
Come on...

683
00:46:41,832 --> 00:46:43,834
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

684
00:46:43,901 --> 00:46:45,002
<i>also known as</i>

685
00:46:45,702 --> 00:46:47,337
<i>Doctor-X.</i>

686
00:46:49,506 --> 00:46:52,209
You could be a model, but you're too old.

687
00:46:52,276 --> 00:46:53,744
I messed up?

688
00:46:53,811 --> 00:46:56,079
Don't fail this time.

689
00:46:56,146 --> 00:46:57,781
Your last chance.

690
00:46:59,550 --> 00:47:00,484
For the patient,

691
00:47:00,551 --> 00:47:01,652
you're the only doctor.

692
00:47:01,718 --> 00:47:03,887
Who is the surgery for?
